{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf6d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a801-0567-73c0-8c2c-4cc236f90421"},"sequence":1553,"recorded_at":1780531400003101,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"98b36224-760c-4ad5-9bfe-0ec4d038663d","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"98b36224-760c-4ad5-9bfe-0ec4d038663d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"98b36224-760c-4ad5-9bfe-0ec4d038663d"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Handed off to review.\n\nRelease run 35040921163 failed in Release prerequisites before any build or signing: the login keychain was locked in the runner session, so notarytool couldn't read the `RunnerControl-notary` profile. No draft or release was created. I repaired the diagnostics rather than the environment: preflight now maps `keychainLocked`, missing-profile, and identity failures to explicit recovery steps, fails fast on zero or multiple team identities, and the DMG signing identity resolves through a tested `release_metadata.py signing-identity` gate called from `release.sh:61`. Recovery is documented in `RELEASING.md`; workflow, tags, releases, runners, and generated files untouched.\n\nEvidence: 16/16 Scripts tests and 12/12 Swift core tests pass, preflight exits 0 locally, 6 narrowing mutants killed with 0 survivors, AC coverage 4 of 8 rows driven by named tests (remainder are historical/external-state bounds with recorded command output). The pending Apple signing-check submission is still In Progress — an external wait, not a blocker. Outcome artifact `TASK-260916-3uyl05_release-ci-signing-and-notary.md` is attached; the candidate is uncommitted in the story worktree for snapshot.","reason":null}}
